From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW4] Settings: no USB entry without UsbService

With android.hardware.bluetooth declared (PW4 Bluetooth), Settings shows the
Connected devices page, whose USB entry builds a UsbBackend and calls
UsbManager.getPorts(). This system has no "usb" service, so getSystemService
returns null and the page crashed on opening (NullPointerException in
UsbBackend.<init>, 2026-11-26, Jump 45). UsbBackend now stops at a missing
UsbManager and says so, and the USB entry is unavailable then.

Not run on the device yet when this patch was written.

--- a/src/com/android/settings/deviceinfo/UsbBackend.java
+++ b/src/com/android/settings/deviceinfo/UsbBackend.java
@@ -61,6 +61,10 @@
         mRestrictedBySystem = userRestrictionUtil.isUsbFileTransferRestrictedBySystem();
         mMidi = context.getPackageManager().hasSystemFeature(PackageManager.FEATURE_MIDI);
 
+        // PW4: no UsbService on this device (no "usb" system service).
+        if (mUsbManager == null) {
+            return;
+        }
         UsbPort[] ports = mUsbManager.getPorts();
         if (ports == null) {
             return;
@@ -78,6 +82,11 @@
         }
     }
 
+    /** PW4: false when the device has no UsbService. */
+    public boolean hasUsbManager() {
+        return mUsbManager != null;
+    }
+
     public int getCurrentMode() {
         if (mPort != null) {
             int power = mPortStatus.getCurrentPowerRole() == UsbPort.POWER_ROLE_SOURCE
--- a/src/com/android/settings/connecteddevice/UsbModePreferenceController.java
+++ b/src/com/android/settings/connecteddevice/UsbModePreferenceController.java
@@ -61,7 +61,9 @@
 
     @Override
     public boolean isAvailable() {
-        return true;
+        // PW4: the Bluetooth feature shows this page; without UsbService the
+        // USB entry has nothing to show and its backend cannot be asked.
+        return mUsbBackend.hasUsbManager();
     }
 
     @Override
